d  import them into link of course i can  only use them for my own purpose i can't  share this in our library because of  copyright reasons however i did approach  assimil and asked them i say you know  isn't there some way we could even sell  your units across our website  uh but no they're not interested in that  um  they should sell the e-text i would  gladly even after having paid for the  book  and the uh the cds  i would gladly have paid for a  transcript of the arabic text  for download but it's not available and  i think so many of these language books  which are very well done  uh  you know very good audio at least in the  case of asimil the audio is excellent  and there's no other language there it's  just arabic  it should be possible to access this  material online i think the textbook  publishers are losing out in that regard  but the online world not only enables  you to access content of interest to you  and a level that's at your level  there's also all of the grammar  resources that are available online not  to mention online dictionaries of which  there are tons and many of them again we  connect with at link  and it's interesting content is so  important to language learning  and  i had an exchange on twitter by the way  where um a teacher at a  english language teaching  conference made a presentation about  how to be a feminist language teacher  and i commented that i didn't think that  this was such a good idea that language  teachers should teach language and  shouldn't teach values however wonderful  these values may be uh and  so there was a bit of a back and forth  about that  and uh one person one language teacher  commented that uh no and and so then i  said they should the teacher should just  allow learners to learn from whatever  they're interested in  and the return comment on that was well  you know in this was in england the  curriculum is such that people have to  study certain items  and i think that's another problem i  think the online  learning world language learning world  makes it possible for  a far greater variety of material to be  used as learning material now you don't  want to make it unlimited if you're in a  school you're limited to a certain range  but it's easy enough  the kids don't have to buy a whole bunch  of textbooks it's easy enough  to  enable them to go and search out things  of interest  and learn from that and use all the  tools that are available online and this  gets back again to the whole issue of  the role of teachers uh changing  while on the subject of online uh  learning uh there was another and again  interaction with people on twitter and  facebook is another  aspect of the sort of online world of uh  of language learning that we're now in  and uh someone pointed out that there  was a teacher or there was a program  where they teach arabic literature  starting with the translation so that  people read  the fable or the poem or whatever it  might be in translation first and then  access it in  arabic  in a way that's a good idea because the  more familiar you are with the content  the easier it is to you know process the  new language  i'm not sure i want to do that myself  because part of the fun of reading  literature is  discovering that piece of work i  wouldn't want to read all of  you know a  ukrainian book on history in english and  then go and read it in ukrainian i would  rather  face that content in ukrainian once i'm  at a level where i can do so  uh on the other hand  a lot of  uh material that is in translation in  fact is quite easy harry potter has been  translated into many languages and for  uh say  many people that's easier  language learning material because  typically translations  are not as  obtuse or as  as  as difficult  to use so but again  with the internet we have a wide variety  of choice and we can learn from what  interests us so just to summarize then  the uh the online experience has  liberated the language learner liberated  the language learner from the classroom  from  imposition of content by the teacher  from the need to buy or borrow books and  cds  you know the world is available at our  fingertips  and we can connect with tutors  uh we can connect with  grammar explanations with content and i  think i've only scratched the surface  so  i encourage people to take advantage of  that  i think historically one of the problems  facing the independent learner the  person who goes once or twice a week to  spanish class and doesn't make much  progress was that sense of being  alone  except when you're in the classroom with  your fellow students and nowadays we can  connect with people all over the world  we can connect with interesting content  all over the world  and  it's great for language learning  so there you go thanks for listening bye  for now  [Music]  you
 

